      "summary": "JavaScript SDK 3.41.0 adds MCP server tracing and changes LiveKit audio capture and upload completion behavior.",
      "body": [
        "Braintrust records AI application activity so engineers can inspect failures and evaluate behavior. JavaScript SDK 3.41.0 adds tracing for Model Context Protocol servers, which expose tools, prompts and resources to AI clients. The linked implementation captures tool calls, prompt retrievals and resource reads, with request and session identifiers for correlation. Tool responses marked isError count as failures even when their handlers do not throw an exception.",
        "The same release fixes a separate evidence gap in LiveKit voice agents. Previously, a job could exit after session.close() resolved while recordings were still uploading. The close now waits for the recording upload. For illustration, an engineer investigating a call should have a better chance of retaining its final recording during a normal close, flush and exit sequence; this does not promise recovery after an arbitrary process crash.",
        "Caller and agent audio now require separate explicit capture flags. The broad attachment setting no longer enables LiveKit audio. The optional @braintrust/audio package adds compressed recordings; without it, the implementation falls back to raw audio. Teams upgrading existing voice instrumentation therefore need to check both consent settings and shutdown behavior."
      ],
